  "notes": "Measured on the A350-1000 ET-BAW (left, 2025-09-01); the fin's bands from the 777F ET-AVT (left, 2026-10-01), whose fin is the same. On the fin the bands keep a white margin to the trailing edge and tip. A small Star Alliance badge and the type name aft are not drawn; some airframes carry temporary '80 years' or '10th A350-1000' decals by the nose, not drawn. Belly white as far as the side photos show. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on ET-BAW (A350-1000, left, 2025-09-01): lengths measured (Ethiopian 0.238, the Amharic 0.074, Ethiopia 0.027, Land of Origins 0.053), serif lowercase 0.62 of the capitals; the fin's three bands are curved sweeps (smooth). Kept on the A350-1000 (drawnOn A35K); Ethiopian's commonest types are the 737 MAX, 787 and Dash 8-400, not re-measured here.",
  "history": "New file (Ethiopian had no scheme here). The tricolor-feather tail and 'Ethiopian' title came with the 2010 rebrand, replacing the earlier scheme with green, yellow and red cheatlines."
